                <pb facs="0934" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg814"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs to Ambassador Meyer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry for Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-06-12"><hi rendition="#italic">June 12/25,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: In response to the memorandum
                    which your excellency has been pleased to address to me this morning, I hasten
                    to inform you that while consenting that the Russian and Japanese
                    plenipotentiaries shall meet at Washington during the first ten days of the
                    month of August, his Majesty the Emperor finds this date rather distant.</p>
                <p>I beg you, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lamsdorff.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
